{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Because of this, that HaShem did for me.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): it means, because HaShem did this for me, therefore I perform this service." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: Scripture says — what HaShem did for me in Egypt, that I went out from Egypt, was for the sake of His name and His glory; and it is like ״זה אלי ואנוהו״ — this is my El and I will glorify Him — which is the Shekhinah up to the supernal Being (havayah). And the intention is that the Shekhinah in Israel is not for the need of an ordinary person alone, but for a supernal need; and this is the matter Joshua said (Joshua 7:9): ״וכרתו את שמנו מן הארץ ומה תעשה לשמך הגדול״ — and they will cut off our name from the earth, and what will You do for Your great name. And understand this, for therefore it is immediately joined to it: ״והיה לך לאות על ידך״ — and it shall be for you a sign upon your hand — and its meaning is, ״והיה זה לך לאות״ — and this shall be for you a sign — upon your hand. And עשה is from the language of (Genesis 41:47) ״ותעש הארץ״, whose Aramaic translation is וכנשת, that is, it gathered into its measures; and this is clear."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:36.396178154Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}